FUN_00448e50: recover the unexported no-op race-event handler

The race-event handler table @0x467084 holds three entries = 0x448e50, an 8-byte empty
function (push ebp; mov ebp,esp; pop ebp; ret) that Ghidra never exported (it sits just
before PitOut @0x448e58). dd2_relocate found no C function at that VA, left the raw x86
address in the table, and Play_Game's event dispatch execute-faulted at 0x448e50 (L1/3-7
frontier). Provide the no-op in dd2h_stubs.c and map it in the dispatch table.

--- a/dd2_dispatch.c
+++ b/dd2_dispatch.c
@@ -490,6 +490,7 @@
 extern int Load_Game_Vags();
 extern int Clear_SoundFx();
 extern int FUN_00448368();
+extern int FUN_00448e50();
 extern int PitOut();
 extern int PitIn();
 extern int Pit_Stop1();
@@ -1355,6 +1356,7 @@
 {0x00448310,(void*)&Load_Game_Vags},
 {0x00448364,(void*)&Clear_SoundFx},
 {0x00448368,(void*)&FUN_00448368},
+{0x00448e50,(void*)&FUN_00448e50},
 {0x00448e58,(void*)&PitOut},
 {0x00448e88,(void*)&PitIn},
 {0x00448f4c,(void*)&Pit_Stop1},
